WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.980
Rocks in Pakistan and Egypt hold fossil whales with leg bones.

2
00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:14.060
Living whales still carry small hip bones inside their bodies.

3
00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:20.280
How can rocks and bones show that whales are related to animals that walked?

4
00:00:21.283 --> 00:00:27.623
Start with rocks. A fossil is the preserved remains or traces of a living thing from

5
00:00:27.623 --> 00:00:31.423
the past. Sedimentary rock builds up in layers.

6
00:00:32.203 --> 00:00:35.563
In an undisturbed stack, the bottom layer came first.

7
00:00:36.023 --> 00:00:38.503
So a fossil in a lower layer is older.

8
00:00:39.243 --> 00:00:40.683
This is relative dating.

9
00:00:41.303 --> 00:00:43.903
It gives an order, not an age in years.

10
00:00:44.817 --> 00:00:47.957
Radioactive dating gives ages in years.

11
00:00:48.977 --> 00:00:51.337
Certain minerals hold radioactive atoms.

12
00:00:52.297 --> 00:00:55.717
These atoms change into other atoms at a steady rate.

13
00:00:56.737 --> 00:01:02.177
Measuring the starting atom left, and the product built up, gives the time since the

14
00:01:02.177 --> 00:01:08.557
mineral formed. Often, volcanic layers above and below a fossil give two dates.

15
00:01:09.297 --> 00:01:11.377
The fossil's age falls between them.

16
00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:15.130
DNA gives a second kind of evidence.

17
00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:21.090
When DNA is copied, small changes sometimes happen, and some are passed on.

18
00:01:22.190 --> 00:01:27.110
Two species that split from a common ancestor recently have had less time to collect

19
00:01:27.110 --> 00:01:33.590
differences. So, for matching stretches of DNA, more similar sequences usually mean

20
00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:35.470
a more recent common ancestor.

21
00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:39.280
Now put the evidence side by side.

22
00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:44.620
Legged whale fossils lie in layers tens of millions of years old.

23
00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:50.960
A vestigial structure is a reduced body part that no longer does the job it did in

24
00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:54.780
ancestors. Living whales have small hip bones.

25
00:01:55.820 --> 00:02:01.140
Vestigial does not mean useless: in males, these bones anchor muscles used in

26
00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:07.200
mating. Pantropical spotted dolphin embryos grow hind-limb buds that break down

27
00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:08.240
around the fifth week.

28
00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:13.320
DNA insertions at the same spots group whales with hippos.

29
00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:15.640
They share a common ancestor.

30
00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:19.720
Each field could have contradicted the others.

31
00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:22.080
For whales, they agree.

32
00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:28.600
Fossils, anatomy, embryos and DNA are independent kinds of evidence.

33
00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:32.020
They point to one history of common descent.

34
00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:36.880
This is why the theory of evolution is a well-tested explanation.

35
00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:41.000
Whales descend from ancestors that walked on land.
